---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { currentReleasePair } from "../data/site";
const windowsInstall = `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process Bypass
.\\install\\install.ps1 -TrustStore C:\\path\\to\\trust-store.json`;
const unixInstall = `sudo ./install/install.sh \\
  --trust-store /path/to/trust-store.json`;
const protectedLaunch = `certael-agent launch \\
  --game /absolute/path/to/exported-game \\
  --trust-store /usr/local/etc/certael/trust-store.json`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Certael Agent — Optional user-mode integrity companion" description="Add fresh signed integrity evidence to Certael protected modes without a kernel driver.">
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Certael Agent · Optional</p>
    <h1>Observe more.<br /><span class="gradient-text">Trust carefully.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Agent is a separately installed user-mode companion. It launches approved builds and signs fresh integrity observations for the authoritative server—without becoming gameplay authority.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="#install">Install Agent</a><a class="button secondary" href={currentReleasePair.agent.url}>Download {currentReleasePair.agent.tag} ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="flow">
      <article><h3>Launch</h3><p>Agent starts an approved game build and establishes private inherited process handles.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Bind</h3><p>The trusted server issues a signed policy and short-lived grant bound to this build and Agent key.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Challenge</h3><p>Fresh server nonces prevent old integrity reports from being replayed as current evidence.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Report</h3><p>The server verifies the signed report chain and classifies the result as client-only evidence.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell" id="install">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Installation</p><h2>One Agent per computer.</h2></div><p>Download the matching {currentReleasePair.agent.tag} archive. The game does not copy Agent into its own directory; the installer places a stable launcher, versioned binary, and public trust store in protected system locations.</p></div>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <article class="prose-card"><p class="eyebrow">Windows 11 x64</p><h3>Elevated PowerShell</h3><ol><li>Extract <code>certael-agent-windows-x86_64.zip</code>.</li><li>Obtain your game operator’s public <code>trust-store.json</code>.</li><li>Open PowerShell as Administrator in the extracted folder.</li></ol><pre><code>{windowsInstall}</code></pre><p>Launcher: <code>C:\Program Files\Certael\certael-agent.exe</code></p></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><p class="eyebrow">Ubuntu 24.04 / macOS 15</p><h3>Root installation</h3><ol><li>Extract the matching x64 or arm64 archive.</li><li>Obtain the operator’s public <code>trust-store.json</code>.</li><li>Run the included installer from the extracted folder.</li></ol><pre><code>{unixInstall}</code></pre><p>Launcher: <code>/usr/local/bin/certael-agent</code></p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">The trust store contains public Ed25519 verification keys only. Never place the signing private key on a player computer or inside the game project.</div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell" id="launch">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Protected launch</p><h2>Let Agent start the export.</h2></div><p>Launch protected online modes through Agent. Start ordinary offline or Agent-disabled modes directly.</p></div>
    <pre><code>{protectedLaunch}</code></pre>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Server prerequisites</h3><ul><li>Core {currentReleasePair.core.tag}</li><li>An approved executable build ID</li><li>A tenant-bound signed Agent policy</li><li>A fresh, short-lived launch grant</li><li>Fresh challenges for every integrity report</li></ul></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Upgrading from Agent alpha.1</h3><ul><li>Stop the old Agent and game first.</li><li>Keep the existing public trust store only if its key remains valid and unrevoked.</li><li>Install the entire {currentReleasePair.agent.tag} archive; do not overwrite only the executable.</li><li>Deploy Core {currentReleasePair.core.tag} and create a new Agent session.</li><li>Do not reuse an alpha.1 policy or launch grant.</li></ul></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Privacy boundary</p><h2>Purposefully limited.</h2></div><p>Agent checks the protected game context. It is not a general surveillance tool and has no kernel component.</p></div>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Agent may report</h3><ul><li>Approved build-file hashes</li><li>Game executable identity</li><li>Game/Agent process relationship</li><li>Loaded image basenames</li><li>Debugger observation and probe health</li></ul></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Agent does not collect</h3><ul><li>Keystrokes or screenshots</li><li>Window titles or unrelated processes</li><li>Network history or raw memory</li><li>Usernames, email, or full command lines</li><li>Arbitrary files outside the approved game</li></ul></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="callout"><strong>Enforcement rule:</strong> a valid Agent report can support observation, sampling, queue restriction, kick, temporary suspension, or manual review according to game policy. Agent-only evidence must never independently produce a permanent account punishment.</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
